# Life Admin — Product Requirements Document

## 1. Product Overview

Life Admin is a web application for managing important personal documents and their renewal/expiry dates in one place.

The product is designed around a real-world problem: people often keep passports, insurance policies, vehicle documents, licences, certificates, warranties, and subscriptions in different places and can miss renewal dates.

The application must provide a useful dashboard, document CRUD, search/filtering, expiry status tracking, validation, secure user ownership, responsive UI, testing, Git/GitHub workflow, and a live deployment.

## 2. Assignment Alignment

The implementation must satisfy the assignment requirements:

- Build a meaningful real-world application rather than a basic to-do/CRUD demo.
- Use Next.js 16 and React.
- Use Tailwind CSS for UI styling.
- Use PostgreSQL or MongoDB as the database. This project standardizes on PostgreSQL.
- Use Git/GitHub for source control and submission.
- Provide a live deployed application.
- Demonstrate robust validation and security.
- Consider performance and optimization.
- Include meaningful testing.
- AI is optional and must remain an additive feature, not a replacement for core functionality.
- Keep the code maintainable and componentized.
- Provide a polished, responsive UI/UX.
- Include the required project/author links in the final application footer.

## 3. Target User

Primary user:
- An individual who needs to track important personal documents and expiry dates.

Example documents:
- Passport
- Driving Licence
- Vehicle Registration
- Car Insurance
- Health Insurance
- Certification
- Warranty
- Subscription
- Other documents with or without expiry dates

## 4. Core User Journey

1. User registers.
2. User logs in.
3. User reaches Dashboard.
4. Dashboard shows document summary and upcoming renewals.
5. User adds a document.
6. User can view, edit, search, filter, sort, and delete documents.
7. System calculates expiry status.
8. User can quickly identify expired and expiring-soon documents.
9. User can review document details.
10. User can log out securely.

## 5. Functional Requirements

### Authentication
- Registration.
- Login.
- Logout.
- Authenticated routes.
- Session-based user identity.
- Every document must belong to one user.

### Dashboard
Display:
- Total document count.
- Expiring-soon count.
- Expired count.
- Upcoming renewal list.
- Quick action to add a document.
- Link to the full Documents page.

### Document CRUD
Create:
- Title.
- Category.
- Document number, optional.
- Issue date, optional.
- Expiry date, optional.
- Notes, optional.

Read:
- List all documents owned by the authenticated user.
- View an individual document.

Update:
- Edit document fields.
- Validate all changed fields.

Delete:
- Require confirmation.
- Delete only documents owned by the authenticated user.

### Search
Search by:
- Document title.
- Document number where available.

### Filters
Category:
- Identity
- Insurance
- Vehicle
- Certification
- Warranty
- Subscription
- Other

Status:
- Active
- Expiring Soon
- Expired
- No Expiry

### Sorting
At minimum:
- Expiry date ascending.
- Expiry date descending.
- Recently updated.

## 6. Expiry Rules

Default status rules:

- EXPIRED: expiry date is before today.
- EXPIRING_SOON: expiry date is today or within the next 30 days.
- ACTIVE: expiry date is more than 30 days away.
- NO_EXPIRY: expiry date is not supplied.

The status calculation must live in a reusable utility/service and must not be duplicated across components.

## 7. Validation Requirements

Backend validation is mandatory.

Use Zod for:
- Required title.
- Valid category.
- Maximum title length.
- Maximum notes length.
- Valid date values.
- Issue date must not be after expiry date when both exist.
- Valid update payloads.

Frontend validation may provide immediate feedback, but backend validation remains authoritative.

## 8. Security Requirements

- Never trust a client-supplied userId.
- Resolve user identity from the authenticated session.
- Every document query must be scoped by authenticated userId.
- Prevent horizontal privilege escalation.
- Return 401 for unauthenticated requests.
- Return 404 when a document is not accessible to the current user.
- Do not expose database errors to end users.
- Do not expose secrets in client-side code.
- Use environment variables for database/auth/API secrets.
- Sanitize and validate all external input.

## 9. Non-Functional Requirements

### UI/UX
- Mobile-first.
- Responsive desktop/tablet/mobile layouts.
- Clear visual hierarchy.
- Accessible form controls.
- Status should use both text and visual styling; color alone must not convey meaning.
- Loading, empty, error, and success states must be handled.

### Performance
- Prefer Next.js Server Components for data-heavy non-interactive UI.
- Use Client Components only where interaction requires them.
- Avoid unnecessary client-side JavaScript.
- Paginate or limit large lists when appropriate.
- Add database indexes for userId and expiryDate.
- Avoid N+1 database queries.
- Use efficient queries for dashboard metrics.

### Maintainability
- Reusable components.
- Typed API contracts.
- Centralized validation.
- Centralized expiry logic.
- Consistent API response shape.
- Clear folder structure.

## 10. Optional AI Feature

An optional AI-assisted "Add with AI" feature may accept user-provided text and extract:
- title
- category
- document number
- issue date
- expiry date

The AI output must always be treated as untrusted input and passed through the same Zod validation before saving.

AI must not be required for the core application to work.

## 11. Main Routes

Pages:
- `/login`
- `/register`
- `/dashboard`
- `/documents`
- `/documents/new`
- `/documents/[id]`
- `/documents/[id]/edit`

API:
- `POST /api/documents`
- `GET /api/documents`
- `GET /api/documents/[id]`
- `PATCH /api/documents/[id]`
- `DELETE /api/documents/[id]`

Recommended:
- `GET /api/dashboard`

## 12. Acceptance Criteria

The project is complete when:

- A user can authenticate.
- A user can create a document.
- A user can see only their own documents.
- A user can edit a document.
- A user can delete a document after confirmation.
- Search works.
- Category/status filters work.
- Expiry status is calculated correctly.
- Dashboard counts are correct.
- Invalid data is rejected.
- Unauthorized access is blocked.
- Responsive UI works on mobile and desktop.
- Meaningful tests pass.
- Application is deployed.
- GitHub repository is available.
- Footer contains required author/project links.
